---
// /community - near-verbatim port of community-8-25 (Jon: "I like almost everything
// about this page"). ONLY the offer/pricing model changes (community-page-spec.md):
// Pricing model (Jon, 2026-08-21): ONE option - a single $291 payment covering
// 3 months, i.e. $97/month paid up front. NOT a subscription. It simply ends;
// members who want to stay opt in to $37/mo afterwards and Jon sends that link
// by hand.
//   - $291 = 3 x $97 ON PURPOSE. It preserves the homepage device ("Either way,
//     you start for $97") where the community and the 1:1 session share an
//     entry price. Do not change one without the other.
//   - LEAD WITH $97/month, $291 as the supporting detail (Jon, 2026-08-23).
//     Matches the homepage door. An earlier version led with $291; the smaller
//     number is the one that gets someone to read the second line.
//   - Always pair "$97/month" with "paid up front" - they must never be
//     separated. Jon: "I don't want it to look like they can sub by the month."
//   - Do NOT say the membership "automatically continues" - nothing renews.
//     Stripe has no record of the 3-month term; a one-time payment has no
//     duration. Jon tracks end dates himself.
//   - NO strikethrough pricing, ever. $291 is the price. Specials are Stripe
//     coupon codes applied at checkout, never a crossed-out number on the page.
//     There is no cheaper community tier - the low-cost door is the $97 1:1
//     session (Jon, 2026-08-21).
// The old "$97/mo x3 or $250 one-pay (save $41)" pair is GONE, along with the
// $147-regular and discount-code apparatus.
// Rationale wording is deliberate: "quitting is a process that takes time" -
// NEVER "that's how long transformation takes", which is a timeline promise and
// violates PRD rule 3. Jon rejected that phrasing explicitly.
// Design: varied treatments per critique - split rows w/ icons, numbered journey,
// ticket pricing. No back-to-back card grids.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import VideoEmbed from '../components/VideoEmbed.astro';
import '../styles/home.css';

// Community video - self-hosted, NOT YouTube (Jon, 2026-08-14).
// Encoded from the 732MB / 15.1 Mbps master down to 44MB / 954 kbps.
// TODO (PRD #15): move these files to Cloudflare R2 and update the paths.

// Checkout for the $291 / 3-month membership. Stripe collects the money; Jon
// then invites them into Mighty Networks BY HAND. Mighty is no longer the
// checkout - the old mn.co/plans/1948481 link sold the retired $97/mo plan.
//
// ✅ LIVE PAYMENT LINK (Jon, 2026-08-25). Created 2026-08-21 and FULLY verified
// via "Pay without Link": $291, correct description, promo codes, no tax row,
// name collection on, consent checkbox linking both Terms and Privacy at their
// working URLs, and the future-payments authorisation that saves the card.
// THIS TAKES REAL MONEY - test cards are declined and any completed checkout
// is a real charge. The build warns if a test link is ever wired back up.
const JOIN_URL = 'https://buy.stripe.com/6oU5kw2k51uBd1scz32oE01';

if (JOIN_URL.includes('/test_')) {
  console.warn(
    '\n⚠️  /community is using a STRIPE SANDBOX link (test_...). ' +
      'It cannot accept real payments. Replace JOIN_URL before launch.\n'
  );
}
---

<Base
  {/* Title rewritten 2026-08-23 for search + AI retrieval. Was "Join the
      AlwaysBeQuitting Community" - the brand name twice and none of the words
      anyone actually searches. The H1 keeps Jon's live-site wording; this is
      metadata, not copy. */}
  title="Quit Smoking or Vaping Together | The ABQ Quitting Community"
  description="Weekly expert coaching and ongoing community support for your quit smoking or vaping journey. $97/month - 3 months, $291 paid up front."
>
  <SiteHeader />

  {/* hero: video + pricing ticket */}
  <header class="band band--teal" style="padding-block: var(--section-sm)">
    <div class="wrap">
      {/* H1 changed 2026-08-23 at Jon's direction. Was "Join the
          AlwaysBeQuitting Community" - verbatim from the live site, but it
          carried the brand name and none of the terms anyone searches. This is
          a DELIBERATE divergence from live-site copy, approved by Jon. */}
      <h1 class="display-xl" style="text-align:center; color:var(--white)">Join the Quit Smoking and Vaping Community</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="font-size: var(--text-lg); color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 85%, transparent)">
        Weekly Expert Coaching + Ongoing Community Support For Your Entire Quit Smoking or Vaping Journey
      </p>
      <div class="hero-split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <VideoEmbed
            src720="/video/community-720p.mp4"
            src480="/video/community-480p.mp4"
            poster="/video/community-poster.webp"
            posterMobile="/video/community-poster-480.webp"
            posterFallback="/video/community-poster.jpg"
            title="Jon introduces the AlwaysBeQuitting community"
          />
        </div>
        <aside class="ticket reveal">
          <p class="ticket__kicker">Full ABQ Community Membership</p>
          <p class="ticket__price">$97<span class="unit">/month</span><span>3 months, $291 paid up front</span></p>
          <p class="ticket__terms">Three months is a commitment to yourself and to the process of quitting, which takes time. <a href="#why-three-months">Why three months?</a></p>
          <p class="ticket__then">After that, you can continue at <strong>$37/month</strong> if you wish.</p>
          <a class="btn btn--cta" href={JOIN_URL}>Join the Community</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  {/* what you get: each feature is its own full-width alternating band */}
  <section class="band band--white" style="padding-block: var(--section-sm) 0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-lg" style="text-align:center">What You Get</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--paper feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="row-split reveal">
        {/* Photos replace icons on rows 1-3 (Jon, 2026-08-23): "I like the
            pictures, I think it makes it more relatable." These are Jon's own
            lead-magnet graphics, already on the live site.

            Row 4 keeps its icon on purpose - there are only three images, and
            Jon found on systeme.io that a fourth pushed unwanted space into the
            next section. Do not hunt for a fourth image. */}
        <picture class="row-split__img">
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/feature-calls.webp 1x, /img/feature-calls@2x.webp 2x" />
          <img src="/img/feature-calls.png" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A laptop showing four people on a live group coaching call" />
        </picture>
        <div>
          <h3 class="rule-heading">Weekly Community Support Calls</h3>
          <p>
            Join Jon for live group coaching - usually one call a week, sometimes more. Ask questions, get guidance
            on whatever you're dealing with that week, and hear from others on the same journey.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Can't make it live?</strong> All calls are recorded and accessible in the community.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--white feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="row-split row-split--flip reveal">
        <picture class="row-split__img">
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/feature-community.webp 1x, /img/feature-community@2x.webp 2x" />
          <img src="/img/feature-community.png" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A laptop showing someone celebrating at sunrise" />
        </picture>
        <div>
          <h3 class="rule-heading">24/7 Community Access</h3>
          <p>
            Connect with others who understand what you're going through. Share wins, get support during struggles,
            and <strong>never feel alone in your quitting journey.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--paper feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="row-split reveal">
        <picture class="row-split__img">
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/feature-accountability.webp 1x, /img/feature-accountability@2x.webp 2x" />
          <img src="/img/feature-accountability.png" width="800" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A laptop showing a completed challenge and progress toolbox" />
        </picture>
        <div>
          <h3 class="rule-heading">Real Accountability Throughout Your Journey</h3>
          <p>
            <strong>Stay motivated and accelerate your commitment to quit.</strong> Post your progress, share
            challenges, get encouragement when you need it most. Jon is active in the community providing guidance
            between calls.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band band--white feature-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      {/* Row 4 has NO icon and NO image (Jon, 2026-08-23). There are only three
          photos - a fourth pushed unwanted space into the next section back on
          systeme.io - and a lone 132px icon beside three 400px photos read as
          inconsistent. Full-width text instead. Do not add an icon back. */}
      <div class="row-split row-split--full reveal">
        <div>
          <h3 class="rule-heading">Build Your Own Plan - Quit at Your Pace</h3>
          <p>You don't follow a one-size-fits-all program (they rarely work). And you don't figure it out alone.</p>
          <p>
            <strong>You create YOUR plan</strong> - when to start, what pace works for your life, whether you take
            big steps, baby steps, or both. <strong>Jon guides you through it</strong> - helping you shape a plan
            that actually works, avoiding the common pitfalls, and supporting you through the countless ways you
            can get derailed.
          </p>
          <p>
            There are millions of ways to fail at quitting. <strong>There are proven ways to succeed.</strong> Our
            unique quitting community can help you find your path through it all.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* four stages: numbered journey */}
  {/* Width override REMOVED 2026-08-23 (Jon). This wrap carried an inline
      max-width:880px with no recorded reason, two-thirds of the site's standard
      1320px. Four cards inside it came out tall and narrow - Jon: "the column
      width is very narrow... they should be more square."

      For reference, the live site runs this section at 1120px with two 540px
      columns. At the standard wrap ours are ~590px, so slightly wider than
      live. Full-bleed was considered and rejected: every other section on the
      site is wrapped, and breaking that here would look accidental. */}
  <section class="band band--paper" style="padding-block: var(--section)">
    <div class="wrap">
      {/* Q and A are a matched pair at the SAME size, as on the live site
           (Jon, 2026-08-14). The Q was previously .kicker - tiny tracked-out
           label type - which buried the teaser under its own answer. */}
      <p class="qa qa--q">
        Q: How do I know if the ABQ community is right for me?
      </p>
      <h2 class="qa qa--a">
        A: Which of these best describes where you are with your smoking or vaping?
      </h2>
      {/* COLLAPSED TO FOUR CHOICES 2026-08-25 (Jon). Each option is a <details>
           whose <summary> is the badge plus the headline; the empathy paragraph
           and the verdict live inside. ALL FOUR CLOSED BY DEFAULT (Jon) - one
           left open would read as the default answer.

           WHY THIS IS NOT AN ORDINARY ACCORDION. The heading above asks "Which
           of these best describes where you are" - so expanding an option IS
           the reader answering the question. The interaction matches the mental
           act, and the A/B/C/D badges (Jon: "it makes it look like it is a
           choice") get stronger when the four headlines sit together as a set
           rather than being buried inside four blocks of body copy.

           THE CLOSER BELOW STILL WORKS AND WAS NOT REWRITTEN. I argued it would
           break - that "whichever you picked, the answer is the same" needs the
           reader to have seen all four verdicts. Jon: "they will have read 4
           titles (four choices)." He is right: the picking happens at the
           HEADLINE level, the verdicts are the answers, not the choices. Do not
           "fix" that line.

           Copy is untouched - every headline, paragraph and verdict is verbatim
           from the previous markup. Content inside <details> stays in the DOM
           and is indexed, so there is no SEO cost on an SEO-sensitive page. */}
      <div class="options">
        <details class="option reveal">
          <summary><span class="option__badge">A</span><h3>You want to quit someday, you just keep putting it off.</h3></summary>
          <p>You feel stuck (like 99.9% of the smokers and vapers on the planet). You're scared to even try to quit. But you have this nagging feeling inside.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>That's okay.</strong> Join now. Use the community and weekly calls to build your confidence and readiness. There's no pressure to quit on day one. Just show up. You'll move forward.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="option reveal">
          <summary><span class="option__badge">B</span><h3>You're finally "ready to quit" and want to set a quit date</h3></summary>
          <p>You've decided - this is it. You want support through the first days, weeks, and months. You may have no idea how to proceed, or you may be crafting a plan.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>Perfect.</strong> You're in charge and we can help get some quitting time under your belt. The community gives you accountability and expert guidance exactly when you need it most.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="option reveal">
          <summary><span class="option__badge">C</span><h3>You've already quit but want to make sure it lasts this time</h3></summary>
          <p>You stopped smoking or vaping, but you're worried about going back. You need accountability to stay quit.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>You're in the right place.</strong> The transformation from temporary abstinence to permanent non-smoker / non-vaper is where most people need the most support. Real transformation takes months. We will be here for you.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="option reveal">
          <summary><span class="option__badge">D</span><h3>You relapsed and want to get back on track</h3></summary>
          <p>You had some smoke-free or vape-free time, but you went back to it. You are on the "quit-relapse" treadmill and you want to get off it.</p>
          <p class="option__verdict"><strong>Don't let shame keep you out.</strong> This is exactly why ongoing support matters. Come back, get motivation from being in the community, fix the things that tripped you up, and start moving forward again.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
      <p style="text-align:center; margin-top: var(--gap-md); font-size: var(--text-base)"><strong>Whichever you picked - the answer is the same. This community was built for exactly where you are.</strong></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* simple truth band */}
  <section class="band band--teal transform">
    <div class="wrap reveal">
      <h2 class="display-lg" style="margin-top: var(--gap-sm)">
        If you're struggling to quit smoking or vaping on your own, joining the ABQ community is the right decision.
      </h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* pricing: ticket, full detail [DIFF: new model, codes removed] */}
  <section class="band band--paper" style="padding-block: var(--section)">
    <div class="wrap wrap--read">
      <div class="ticket ticket--big reveal">
        <p class="ticket__kicker">Full ABQ Community Membership</p>
        <p class="ticket__price">$97<span class="unit">/month</span><span>3 months, $291 paid up front</span></p>
        <p class="ticket__terms">
          Three months is a commitment to yourself and to the process of quitting, which takes time.
        </p>
        {/* Rewritten 2026-08-23 (Jon). Was "The longer you stay, the cheaper it
            gets - the opposite of every program that's burned you." That scored
            a point against competitors instead of explaining the motive. The
            price drops because Jon wants people to stay as long as they need,
            and saying so plainly is warmer and more believable. */}
        <p class="ticket__then">
          After your 3 months, you can continue at <strong>$37/month if you wish</strong>. We reduce the price
          because we want you to stay for as long as you need to - many people need the accountability, and
          plenty of them simply love the community.
        </p>
        {/* "No refunds on the $291" removed here (Jon): it reads harsh on a card
            that is asking someone to join. The refund policy is stated plainly
            in the subscription/cancellation FAQ, which is where someone worried
            about it will look. Do not put it back on the ticket. */}
        <p class="ticket__alt">
          Your commitment to transformation is 3 months. After that, it's up to you whether you continue. <a href="#why-three-months">Why three months?</a>
        </p>
        {/* checks--ink removed 2026-08-26: it was only ever DEFINED in
            coaching.astro's scoped style block, so Astro scoping meant it
            could never apply here. Harmless - this page's own .checks already
            renders dark text with teal ticks on a white band. */}
        <ul class="checks">
          <li>24/7 access to community support</li>
          <li>Community Support Calls - usually one a week, schedule published at the start of each month</li>
          <li>Access to call recordings + ability to ask questions beforehand</li>
          <li>Accountability check-ins (voluntary and without shock collars 🙂)</li>
          <li>Expert guidance on withdrawal, mindset, and behavior change</li>
          <li>Quit at your pace - no rigid timeline to follow</li>
          <li>Positive, committed community (no lurkers or trial members)</li>
        </ul>
        <a class="btn btn--cta" href={JOIN_URL} style="align-self:center">Join the Community</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* just start / antidote close */}
  <section class="band band--white" style="padding-block: var(--section); text-align:center">
    <div class="wrap wrap--read">
      {/* OBJECTION HANDLER, not a value-prop section (Jon, 2026-08-23). Its one
          job: "combat the belief held by smokers and vapers that they CAN'T
          afford programs like this. When they can."

          Everything here serves that and should be left alone:
            - "Just Start." answers the objection's real conclusion - "so I'll
              wait until I can afford it." It is not an orphaned CTA heading.
            - "insane value" is the claim being made, not hype. Do not soften it
              on voice.md grounds; in an affordability argument it is the point.
            - Small paragraph then large: the money math is the setup, "you're
              already spending the money" is the payoff and only lands because
              the figure came first. Do not equalise them or split them into two
              sections - that separates the punch from what powers it.

          Placement before the CTA is deliberate: StoryBrand handles the
          objection immediately before the ask. */}
      <h2 class="display-lg">Just Start.</h2>
      {/* WEIGHTING REVERSED 2026-08-23 at Jon's direction: the value paragraph
          is now the LARGE one and "you're already spending the money" is the
          smaller follow-on.

          This overrides my recommendation, which was to keep the second larger
          on setup-then-payoff grounds. Jon's call, and it follows from the
          section's job: the objection is "I can't afford this", so the figure
          that defeats it should be the loudest thing here. Do not swap them
          back.

          It was previously 1.15rem in --soft grey, which is the page's skip-me
          styling - the sentence carrying the proof was the one being skipped. */}
      <p class="display-lg statement" style="margin-top: var(--gap-sm); font-size: var(--display-sm); color:var(--ink)">
        The ABQ community is an insane value. <strong>Most people spend hundreds a month</strong> on smoking or vaping - <em>you'll save hundreds of thousands over your lifetime by quitting.</em>
      </p>
      {/* Rewritten 2026-08-23 (Jon). CAPS on CHOICE are his emphasis, as in the
          "FOCUS ON QUITTING" line in the FAQ - keep them as typed.

          NOTE: this drops "we are the antidote to those companies", which
          voice.md lists as a signature phrase and community-page-spec calls the
          "antidote close". Flagged to Jon; the replacement moves from
          positioning against competitors to putting the decision in the
          reader's hands, which suits an objection handler better. */}
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top: var(--gap-md); font-size: var(--text-base); line-height:1.6; color:var(--ink)">
        You're already spending the money. Every day you make a CHOICE to give money to companies that are making
        you sick. Today can be the day that you make the CHOICE to change that.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* testimonials */}
  {/* Testimonials are DELIBERATELY SHORTER here than on the homepage (Jon,
       2026-08-23), which carries the same three at full live-site length. Not
       an inconsistency to fix, for two reasons:

       1. They are placeholders. Community-member testimonials replace these as
          they arrive - Jon: "as i get community testimonials, I will replace
          them." Until then, 1:1 proof stands in.
       2. The cuts are good. Katherine's keeps both load-bearing lines - "it
          took me nearly six years to build the courage" and "if you have
          reservations about investing in a coach, I cannot recommend Jon
          enough" - and drops only the middle.

       DO NOT lengthen these to match the homepage. */}
  <section class="band band--paper proof">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top: var(--gap-md)">
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>It took me nearly six years to build the courage to find a specialist and I am unbelievably grateful it was Jon. If you have reservations about investing in a coach, I cannot recommend Jon enough. The impact he has had on my life is transformative.</blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            <picture>
              <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/katherine-headshot.webp" />
              <img class="quote__photo" src="/img/katherine-headshot.jpg" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Katherine" />
            </picture>
            <span><b>Katherine</b> · One Year Vape Free</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>Jon's non-assuming approach and meeting me where I was at was really helpful. Having the support and the accountability - it's kind of two sides of the same coin. That was probably one of the pieces that I was missing.</blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            <picture>
              <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/kait-headshot.webp" />
              <img class="quote__photo" src="/img/kait-headshot.jpg" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Kait" />
            </picture>
            <span><b>Kait</b> · 9 Years Sober, Now Smoke-Free</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="card quote reveal">
          <blockquote>I've invited Jon to teach about tobacco treatment to my "Health Counseling" university class for 9 straight semesters. His presentations are informative, entertaining and inspiring.</blockquote>
          <figcaption>
            <picture>
              <source type="image/webp" srcset="/img/ashley-headshot.webp" />
              <img class="quote__photo" src="/img/ashley-headshot.jpg" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Ashley Foster, MPH, RD, CHES" />
            </picture>
            <span><b>Ashley Foster</b> · MPH, RD, CHES · University Professor</span>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* FAQ - verbatim except subscription item [DIFF] */}
  <section class="band band--white">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <h2 class="display-lg">Common Questions</h2>
      {/* VERBATIM from the live site (Jon, 2026-08-14). A previous rewrite
           flattened both bulleted lists into run-on sentences and dropped the
           judgment-free line and the consulting/training note. Keep the lists. */}
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>Who can join ABQ programs and community?</summary>
        <p>
          This community is for people who smoke or vape and want to quit - or who recently quit and need support
          to stay quit.
        </p>
        <p><strong>You're welcome to join if you are:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Currently use tobacco, nicotine, or vaping products and want to quit</li>
          <li>Recently quit but are struggling to maintain it</li>
          <li>Relapsed and need support to get back on track</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>To maintain a focused, supportive environment, we don't allow:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Healthcare professionals (unless you're personally seeking help for your own tobacco/nicotine use, and inform us of it)</li>
          <li>Anyone affiliated with the tobacco, nicotine, or vaping industry</li>
          <li>People looking to learn our methods for their own coaching, training, or business purposes</li>
          <li>Anyone misrepresenting their tobacco/nicotine use status</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          <strong>Why?</strong> Our community thrives when everyone is genuinely focused on their own quitting
          journey. This creates the judgment-free environment that helps people succeed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Violating these requirements results in immediate removal with no refund, as outlined in our complete <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Note:</strong> If you're interested in our training methods for professional purposes, we offer
          separate consulting and training services. Feel free to contact us directly to discuss those options.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>When do the Community Support Calls happen? What if I miss one?</summary>
        <p>
          <strong>Current Schedule:</strong> Community Support Calls are scheduled at the beginning of the month.
          There is usually one per week, sometimes more.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Please note:</strong> We try to choose different times of the day so that both US and
          international members have a chance to attend. We publish the schedule at the beginning of each month.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Can't make it live?</strong> All calls are recorded and available to watch later. You can also
          submit questions ahead of time, and Jon will answer them during the call even if you can't attend live.
        </p>
        <p>
          Plus, you have 24/7 access to the community where you can get support, ask questions, and connect with
          others any time.
        </p>
      </details>
      {/* Added 2026-08-23 (Jon). Placed BEFORE "how long should I stay" because
           it answers the objection the price raises - why can't I just try a
           month - and that question comes first for someone reading the ticket.

           Carries the second rationale Jon parked on 2026-08-21: the commitment
           is also what keeps the room full of people who mean it. Written as a
           member benefit, never as gatekeeping.

           NO TIMELINE PROMISE. "Quitting is a process that takes time" is the
           approved wording; "because that's how long transformation takes" is
           banned - see PRD rule 3 and community-page-spec. */}
      <details class="reveal" id="why-three-months">
        <summary>Why do you require three months?</summary>
        <p>
          Two reasons. <strong>The first is you.</strong> Quitting is a process that takes time, and the hardest
          stretch usually comes after the newness wears off - which is exactly when people walk away from support.
          Paying up front means that decision is already made, and you're still here for the part that matters most.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The second is everyone else.</strong> A three-month commitment means the people in the room are
          people who mean it. No lurkers, no one dipping a toe in for a week. You'll be alongside others who have
          made the same decision you have, and that changes what the group is worth to you.
        </p>
        <p>
          {/* Keep "a" and the link on ONE line. Astro's compressHTML strips the
              newline + indent between an inline element and the word before it,
              so a line break here renders as "and aone-time". */}
          If you'd rather not commit to three months, that's a completely reasonable answer - and <a href="/coaching">a one-time $97 session with me</a> is probably the better place to start.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>How long should I stay in the community?</summary>
        <p>
          <strong>The short answer:</strong> as long as you need. <strong>The realistic answer:</strong> real
          transformation typically takes 3–6 months, especially for longer-term smokers and vapers - that's exactly
          why membership starts with a 3-month commitment. Let's face it: things are going to come up. If you want
          the best shot at quitting for life, don't focus on quitting the community. <strong>FOCUS ON QUITTING smoking or vaping for life. That is the end game.</strong> After your first
          3 months, you can continue at just $37/month if you wish - and how long you stay is entirely up to you.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>What's your subscription, cancellation, and refund policy?</summary>
        <p>
          <strong>Your membership:</strong> ABQ Community membership is one payment of $291 - $97/month for 3 months,
          paid up front. All 3 months are yours and the payment stands; we
          don't offer refunds for any reason. This isn't because we don't stand behind what we do - it's because
          transformation requires commitment, and an "easy out" encourages giving up exactly when things get
          challenging. <strong>After 3 months:</strong> your membership ends unless you choose to continue. If you
          want to stay, it's $37/month for as long as you like - just let me know and I'll send you the link. <strong>What we guarantee:</strong> the
          delivery of weekly Community Support Calls, ongoing community access, and Jon's guidance. <strong>What we can't guarantee:</strong> that you'll quit. Your success depends on factors under your
          control - your mindset, decisions, commitment, and how you navigate the challenges. We provide guidance,
          accountability, and support, but we can't execute the process for you. We think you can do this!
        </p>
      </details>
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>Is this community confidential?</summary>
        <p><strong>No, this community is NOT confidential like a doctor's office or therapist's office.</strong></p>
        <p>Here's what that means:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Other members will see what you post in the community</li>
          <li>Other members will hear what you say on Community Support Calls</li>
          <li>We can't control what others remember or discuss outside the community</li>
          <li>This is peer support and coaching - not medical or therapeutic care with confidentiality protections</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Only share what you're comfortable with others knowing.</strong></p>
        <p>
          If you need medical care or therapy with full confidentiality protections, please seek those services
          from licensed healthcare professionals.
        </p>
        <p>
          For complete medical disclaimers, liability limitations, and additional legal protections, please see our
          full <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
      {/* MEDICAL DISCLAIMER - VERBATIM from the live site (Jon, 2026-08-14).
           Restored in full after a condensed rewrite dropped roughly two-thirds
           of it, including the entire "Medication Discussions" and "Our
           Commitment to You" sections. DO NOT edit, shorten, or "tidy" this
           text. Legal/medical wording is never changed on a judgment call. */}
      <details class="reveal">
        <summary>Medical Disclaimer</summary>
        <p>
          We know this isn't the most exciting thing to read, but we need to be crystal clear about what we offer
          and what we don't.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What We Provide</strong><br />
          All of our services—coaching, community support, and educational materials—are for information and
          education only. We're here to provide guidance, support, accountability, and proven strategies to help
          you on your quitting journey.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>What We Don't Provide</strong><br />
          Our services are NOT medical, mental health, or addiction treatment. We are not doctors, therapists, or
          medical professionals. Our coaching and community do not constitute medical care. While we're passionate
          about helping you quit and have extensive experience in this area, we cannot replace professional
          healthcare.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Your Responsibility</strong><br />
          It's your responsibility to verify with your doctor, healthcare provider, or therapist that our
          information and guidance are appropriate for your specific situation. You assume all responsibility for
          how you apply what you learn in our programs.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>When to Seek Medical Care</strong><br />
          If you're experiencing thoughts of self-harm, severe depression, serious physical symptoms, or any mental
          health crisis, please seek immediate professional medical attention. Call 911 in any emergency situation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Medication Discussions</strong><br />
          We may discuss various cessation aids, medications, and products as educational information only. Any
          medication decisions must be made in consultation with qualified healthcare professionals. We are not
          prescribing or personally recommending specific medications for your individual use.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Our Commitment to You</strong><br />
          While we can't provide medical treatment, we are absolutely committed to providing you with the best
          educational resources, coaching support, and community encouragement to help you succeed in your quitting
          journey. We believe in your ability to quit, and we're here to support you every step of the way!
        </p>
        <p>
          If you want medical care or mental health treatment, we encourage you to pursue that with professional
          treatment facilities and providers.
        </p>
        <p>
          For complete medical disclaimers, liability limitations, and additional legal protections, please see our
          full <a href="/terms">Terms and Conditions</a>.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* final cta */}
  <section class="band band--teal final">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="display-xl hl">Finally become the non-smoker or non-vaper <em>you dreamed about.</em></h2>
      <p style="margin-top: var(--gap-sm); font-size: var(--text-base); color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white) 85%, transparent)">
        Imagine waking up breathing freely. Not thinking about when you can smoke or vape next. Not hiding it or
        making excuses. Not spending hundreds every month on something that's hurting you. <strong style="color:var(--white)">That's what transformation looks like. You can do this.</strong>
      </p>
      <div class="final__actions reveal">
        <a class="btn btn--cta" href={JOIN_URL}>Join the Community</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SiteFooter />
  {/* Both price cards link to #why-three-months. A <details> is closed by
      default, so jumping to it would otherwise scroll to a collapsed answer.
      This opens it on arrival, and on any later in-page click. */}
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      function openTarget() {
        var el = document.getElementById(location.hash.slice(1));
        if (el && el.tagName === 'DETAILS') el.open = true;
      }
      openTarget();
      window.addEventListener('hashchange', openTarget);
    })();
  </script>
</Base>

